description:
## Objective
Make Setup the main screen of the "Beads Manager" surface: title "Beads Manager", a "Workspaces" button, no back button, version line at the bottom. Move today's workspace list behind that button as a secondary view with a ← back to Setup. Show the status strip (slash-command notice, old-host warning, Manager-launch state) on both views.

## Context
The owner wants Beads Manager to open straight on its configuration (beads tools, agent skills, extra role instructions), which today sits behind a ⚙ icon. The owner also wants to lose nothing of the workspace list: pins, running dot, bead figures, Go to / Metric / Beads, and history of closed workspaces (decisions Q1 a, Q6 a). `/bm-worker-stop-all` posts its notice to the surface and opens it, and the Command Center "Open Beads Manager" launch runs in any view. So the notices must show on the new main screen too.

## Scope
In:
- the surface's view names and default;
- back navigation;
- the status strip, as a pure function plus one component placed in two views;
- the Setup screen's header, intro line and version line;
- the workspace list's header;
- tests.

Out:
- the content of Setup below its header (tools, skills, instructions);
- the rows of the workspace list;
- the Metric/Beads screens;
- Command Center items and slash commands (their behaviour and texts stay);
- the "+" panel (another leaf);
- row colours (another leaf).

## Components Touched
- `plugin/client/dashboard-view.ts`:
  - `DashboardViewName` becomes `"setup" | "workspaces" | "dashboard" | "beads"`;
  - `export const SURFACE_HOME_VIEW: DashboardViewName = "setup"`;
  - `export function backOf(view)`: `"dashboard"` and `"beads"` → `"workspaces"`, `"workspaces"` → `"setup"`, `"setup"` → `null`.
- `plugin/client/launch-manager.ts` (pure):
  - `export const OLD_HOST_WARNING = "This Paseo version cannot open agents from plugins. Update Paseo to use this launcher."` — the exact text `launcher.tsx` shows today;
  - `export interface StatusLine { key: string; text: string; tone: NoticeTone; dismissable: boolean }`;
  - `export function launcherStatusLines({ commandNotice, canOpenAgents, state })` returns, in order:
    1. the command notice if non-null (tone `muted`, `dismissable: true`);
    2. `OLD_HOST_WARNING` when `!canOpenAgents` (tone `warning`);
    3. each line of `describeLauncherState(state)` with its own tone.

    Only line 1 is dismissable.
- `plugin/client/launcher.tsx`:
  - `useState(SURFACE_HOME_VIEW)`;
  - new component `LauncherStatus({ lines, onDismiss, theme, styles })`: a dismissable line is a `Pressable` with accessibility label `"<text>. Dismiss."` that calls `launcherNotices.take()`, as today; the other lines are `Text` with `accessibilityLiveRegion="polite"` coloured by `toneColor`;
  - build it ONCE as `const status = <LauncherStatus … />` and use it in exactly two places: `<SetupScreen … onOpenWorkspaces={() => setView("workspaces")} status={status} />` for view `"setup"`, and `{status}` right under the header inside the workspace list's `ScrollView`;
  - the workspace list's header becomes `[←] Workspaces` (accessibility label "Back to Beads Manager setup"), and the ⚙ button is removed;
  - the Metric/Beads screens opened from the list get `onBack={() => setView("workspaces")}`;
  - the three inline notice blocks of the list are replaced by `{status}`;
  - keep the `dashboardRequests` effect and the `runPendingRequest` effect as they are (with the new view names).
- `plugin/client/setup-screen.tsx`:
  - `SetupScreenProps` = `PluginSurfaceProps & { onOpenWorkspaces: () => void; status?: ReactNode }`; `onBack` removed;
  - header row: title "Beads Manager" (flex 1), then a `secondaryButton` "Workspaces" with accessibility label "Open the workspace list: Beads Manager, metrics and beads of each workspace";
  - next, one body line "Setup for this machine: beads tools, agent skills and extra instructions for each role.";
  - then `status`;
  - then today's content unchanged;
  - last, a footer `paseo-bm ${PLUGIN_VERSION}` (import from `../shared/version`).
- `test/plugin-dashboard-view.test.ts` — `SURFACE_HOME_VIEW` and `backOf` for all four views.
- `test/plugin-launcher.test.ts`:
  - `launcherStatusLines` cases;
  - a placement case that reads `plugin/client/launcher.tsx` as text (like `test/plugin-structure.test.ts` reads files) and asserts: exactly one `<LauncherStatus` occurrence, `status={status}` inside the `<SetupScreen` element, and `{status}` in the workspace-list branch.

## Dependencies / Prerequisites
none. (Sequenced after the WP-261 leaf only to avoid editing `dashboard-view.ts` and its test at the same time.)

## Assumptions / Constraints
- `SetupScreen` is only rendered by `launcher.tsx`; no other caller needs `onBack`.
- Notice texts do not change. `test/plugin-slash-commands.test.ts` must stay green without changing its expectations.
- Metric and Beads views do not show the status strip (as today).
- `test/plugin-launcher.test.ts` loads every client `.tsx` with `vi.mock("react-native")` providing only `ActivityIndicator`, `Pressable`, `ScrollView`, `Text`, `View`. No module-level use of any `react-native` value.
- No file under `test/` imports `react-native` as a value. `.tsx` modules are loaded through a non-literal specifier.
- React Native primitives only, colours from `theme.colors`, no web-only constructs, no `server/` import.
- Another Worker (req-20260918T041426Z) edits `chat-cards.ts` / `chat-card.tsx` / `roles/*.md`: do not touch them. Run `git status` before starting.

## Acceptance Criteria
- `SURFACE_HOME_VIEW === "setup"`; `backOf("dashboard") === "workspaces"`, `backOf("beads") === "workspaces"`, `backOf("workspaces") === "setup"`, `backOf("setup") === null`.
- `launcherStatusLines`:
  - nothing to say → `[]`;
  - a command notice → first line, `dismissable: true`;
  - `canOpenAgents: false` → a line with exactly `OLD_HOST_WARNING`, tone `warning`;
  - states `pending`, `error`, `opened` (with other Managers) → exactly the `describeLauncherState` lines after the other two, with their tones;
  - only the notice line is dismissable.
- Placement: exactly one `<LauncherStatus` in `launcher.tsx`, `status={status}` on `<SetupScreen`, and `{status}` in the list branch. Negative control: removing `{status}` from the list branch makes the placement case fail (observed red, then restored).
- The surface opens on Setup, titled "Beads Manager", with a "Workspaces" button, no ←, and the version line. "Workspaces" opens the unchanged list with ← back to Setup; Metric/Beads from the list go ← back to the list.
- `test/plugin-slash-commands.test.ts` passes with no expectation changed.

## Validation / Definition of Done
- `npm test -- test/plugin-dashboard-view.test.ts test/plugin-launcher.test.ts test/plugin-slash-commands.test.ts test/plugin-launcher-order.test.ts test/plugin-launcher-running-dot.test.ts test/plugin-structure.test.ts` exits 0.
- `npm run typecheck:plugin` exits 0.
- `npm run typecheck` exits 0.
- `npm run lint` exits 0.

## Primary Proof
The new `backOf`, `launcherStatusLines` and placement cases green, with the placement negative control seen red, plus `npm run typecheck:plugin` exit 0 for the `.tsx` changes. The visual check is the owner's real-daemon run.

## Reversibility
Revert the files above. No persisted data (the pinned order file is untouched). The running plugin changes only when the owner reloads it.

## Provenance
Request: req-20260918T043115Z — "Đổi lại UX, Màn hình chính của Bead Manager sẽ không thể hiện như hiện tại nữa, mà hãy thể hiện luôn phần config cho Bead Manager"
Source: docs/plans/paseo-bm-implementation-plan-delta-20260918e-beads-tab.md#WP-262
Requirements: REQ-060 (d), (e), (f)
Design refs: docs/design/paseo-bm-delta-20260918e-beads-tab.md §2 F7, §4.2, §6

## Purpose
Batch b4 of Phase 2a-9, asked by the owner after the first delivery (decisions Q8–Q12): on the Beads screen, colour the bead title instead of the whole row, split the list into In progress → Blocked → Ready → Closed groups, hide closed beads behind an eye toggle, show "✓ done / total" at the top, and drop the "Created / closed, last 14 days" chart.

## Scope
Four leaves under WP-264:
- title colour (Beads list and the "Beads in this chat" panel);
- groups plus the eye toggle;
- the quick done/total figure plus removing the 14-day chart;
- re-applying REQ-060 to the Dashboard PRD and verifying the package.

Out of scope:
- persisting the eye state across app reloads;
- groups or an eye toggle in the chat panel;
- the "+" tab and the surface;
- `beadsOverview` internals;
- chat-card files;
- version bump, release, commit.

## Success Criteria
- All four leaves closed with evidence.
- `npm run verify` exits 0.
- The owner's real-daemon check (desktop and phone) happens after `finished`; no bead waits on it.

